  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-10T19:20:15.668Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When creating a toggle in a submenu, the parameter that controls is must be a stage in both the submenu and main menus stageparams. If the parameter is a stage on only the submenus stageparams the toggle will not function. I've only tested this with buttons and toggles, so I don't know if this happens with any other control type.\nThe 3.0 avatar walkthrough - part 4 - says though you can make submenus within submenus \"And so on. And so on, and so on, and so on… its turtles all the way down, baby!\" Forcing a parameter to be featured on both stageparams makes this claim impossible because the stageparams are limited to 16 stages, and the main menus stageparams will quickly be filled by the submenus parameters. So I assume this is a bug.",
